\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 
Mrs Susie Kind arrived on the Wednesday at ten, in a good coat, with a wheeled document case and an air of a woman braced for the kindly, hurried explanation of why she had wasted her time. She was fifty-eight. She apologised twice for the case.
\par "I want to say at the start that I know what I sound like," she said. "I have a brochure business and a strong opinion about the universe. I am aware of the type."
\par "Mrs Kind," said Fainrose, "I have read your eleven pages four times. Two of your steps are wrong and one of them is wrong in an interesting way. Sit down. What made you start?"
\par Mrs Kind put the case on the table and did not open it.
\par "Baggage," she said.
\par "Baggage."
\par "In nineteen ninety-nine I began keeping a note of the complaints, because complaints are the only honest data a travel agent gets. Nobody writes in to say the week was exactly as advertised." She folded her hands. "And after some years I noticed that I c
ould predict the complaint from the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 booking form}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 
. Not from the destination, not from the price, not from the hotel. From the form. From how much of the form the client had filled in and which boxes they had left as }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 
no preference}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 ."
\par Neville said, "Go on."
\par "A client who specifies eleven things will complain about a twelfth. A client who specifies nothing will come home content, and will not be able to tell you the name of the town." She looked up. "And I thought: the holiday I am selling is not in Spain. It
 is on that form. The form has an area \emdash  it has boxes, a finite number, and each box holds one answer \emdash  and }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 
everything the client will ever be able to say about the fortnight has to fit in those boxes.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567  If it isn't on the form it doesn't happen to them. It happens near them."
\par Miss Pike, who had come in halfway through with coffee for four and had not sat down, said, "That's a bound."
\par "I beg your pardon?"
\par "You've described a bound. The amount that can be true inside the holiday is limited by the size of the surface you wrote it on."
\par Mrs Kind looked at her for a moment with the expression of a person hearing her own accent for the first time in twenty years.
\par "Yes," she said. "That is exactly what I have been unable to say."
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 
