\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 Halpert Weinstein telephoned at half past eleven, which he had never done, and would not say how he had the number.
\par "They have told you about the wall," he said.
\par "A travel agent told us about the wall."
\par "Of course she did." A sound that might have been satisfaction. "Mr Wren, I want to say one thing and then I want to go and lie down, because I am still thin. You will now believe that nothing was destroyed, because on this account nothing ever is 
\emdash  the information is on the surface, the surface was rewritten, the accounts balance, and Tegn\'e9r will be in the newspapers within a fortnight explaining that there is therefore no wrong to remedy."
\par "And?"
\par "And he will be correct and it will be the most successful lie of the decade," said Weinstein. "Because I was }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 there}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
