\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 Neville wrote, at midnight, in volume five:
\par Not volume. Area.\line Everything true in here is already written on the walls.\line The inside is a way of reading the outside.
\par Then:
\par Nothing did not get cheaper.\line There was less written on the wall.\line Ninety minutes to clear. Three hours to write. Ninety to reconcile.
\par Then, underlined twice:
\par They took the thinnest records because they were the cheapest to clear.\line We made them thin. On purpose. With a form. Monthly.
\par Then:
\par The Statement of Coherence is a picking list.
\par And last:
\par 9 February.\line Make everybody fat.\line Give them somewhere real they could still go.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs36\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 
Physics
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 Chapter Four carries the }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 holographic principle}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 , and the entropy bounds that force it.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 The bound that starts it.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 
 Ordinary intuition says the information capacity of a region scales with its volume. Bekenstein's 1972 work on black hole thermodynamics broke that. A black hole's entropy is proportional not to its volume but to the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 area of its event horizon}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 :
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\tx916\tx1832\tx2748\tx3664\tx4580\tx5496\tx6412\tx7328\tx8244\tx9160\tx10076\tx10992\tx11908\tx12824\tx13740\tx14656\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs20\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 S_\{\\text\{BH\}\} = \\frac\{k_B c^3 A\}\{4 G \\hbar\} = \\frac\{k_B A\}\{4 \\ell_P^2\}
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 
one quarter of a bit per Planck area, where }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs20\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 \\ell_P = \\sqrt\{\\hbar G / c^3\} \\approx 1.6 \\times 10^\{-35\}\\,\\text\{m\}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 . Since a black hole is the highest-entropy object that fits in a given region \emdash  try to exceed it and the region collapses into one \emdash 
 the area expression is not merely the capacity of black holes. It is the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 capacity of space}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 
. This is the Bekenstein bound, later sharpened by Bousso into a covariant statement about light-sheets that survives in cosmological settings.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 From a bound to a principle.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567  
't Hooft and Susskind took the further step: if everything that can be true inside a region fits on its boundary, the most economical reading is that the boundary description is not a summary but a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 complete, equivalent}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 
 account. The interior, with its three dimensions and its gravity, is that same information encoded in a form you can walk about in. The concrete realisation is the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 
AdS/CFT correspondence}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567  
(Maldacena, 1997): a gravitational theory in a (d+1)-dimensional anti-de Sitter bulk is exactly dual to a conformal field theory without gravity on its d-dimensional boundary. Two descriptions, one physics. Neither is the "real" one.
\par This is Mrs Kind's holiday. Two hotels producing an identical set of relations are not two holidays with a hidden fact about which you were in. There is no further fact. Duality is that claim, made precise.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 Why a travel agent, and why baggage.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567  
The chapter's device is not arbitrary. Mrs Kind arrives at the bound through the observation that everything a client can ever report has to fit in the boxes of a booking form \emdash 
 a finite surface constraining an apparently unbounded interior experience. Leonard Susskind was a plumber before he was a physicist; the through-line of these books is that the people who noticed the strange thing were rarely the ones trained not to.

\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 The mechanism she proposes.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567  Her physical claim \emdash 
 that the vacuum did not become cheaper but rather }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 less subscribed}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567  \emdash 
 is speculative fiction built on a real relationship. Vacuum energy and horizon entropy are not independent: in de Sitter space the horizon carries entropy }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs20\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 S = A/4\\
ell_P^2}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567  and a temperature }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs20\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 T = H/2\\pi}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 
, and the cosmological constant, the horizon area, and the information capacity are locked together. A local reduction in the information written on a screen is, in that framework, a local change in what the vacuum costs. The ramp-plateau-ramp profile fro
m Chapter Two is then not a wave traversing the region \emdash  it is the signature of a clear, a write, and a reconciliation, which is exactly why it has a duration and a symmetric shape rather than a dispersion.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 The entropy accounting.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567  The chapter's arithmetic is deliberately loose and says so \emdash 
 a factor of two, order }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs20\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 10^\{57\}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 
 bits. The point is not the number but the argument: a pending state with two live options is a fat record, because it must encode both branches and every correlation with parties awaiting the answer. A pending state whose options have both become impossi
ble encodes almost nothing. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 The Ministry's own nineteen months of tidy monthly returns thinned those fourteen records to near-minimal surface content}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 
, which made them the cheapest area on the wall to clear. This is Kastner's rule from Book One arriving with a bill: the institution that promised to make things simple had moved the complexity somewhere it could not see, and something else read the recei
pt.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 The defence, and why it is real physics as well as good ethics.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567  
"Make everybody fat" is Mrs Kind's operational recommendation, and it follows from the same accounting. A record carrying live, reachable options has high surface content and high correlation with its environment, and is therefore both expensive to clear 
and \emdash  recalling Chapter One \emdash  separated from the outside of the register by a genuine barrier rather than an administrative one. Restoring a real option to a person is, in this framework, literally a hardening measure.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 What Weinstein is warning about.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567  
The holographic principle is the strongest available answer to the black hole information paradox: nothing is destroyed, because the interior was never independent of the surface. That is a genuine resolution and it is why Tegn\'e9
r will be right in the newspapers. But unitarity guarantees only that information is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 conserved}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 
, not that it remains }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567 accessible to you}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid15733567  \emdash 
 and Weinstein's testimony is that the fourteen produced no discarded branches at all, which is not the signature of destruction but of transfer. Conservation with a change of custody is the through-line of both books, and it is not a comfort.
