The Galactic Counsel is not called that because of any galaxy. It is called that because in 1961 a clerk in the Cabinet Office was handed a treaty instrument in a language nobody could read and asked to file it, and he filed it under Counsel, meaning advi
ce, and the misspelling entered the schedule, and the schedule entered the Act, and by the time anybody noticed there had been eleven cross-references and it was easier to leave it.
\par Neville learned this from Mrs Kind, on a Thursday, because Mrs Kind read footnotes.
\par "It's a body of advisers, not a council of worlds," she said. "That's the whole difference and everyone gets it wrong including them. It has no army and no territory and no money of its own. What it has is the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
