\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 The papers came through Weinstein, who had observer status, which he described as "the status of a creature too old to exclude and too disreputable to consult."
\par There were three of them.
\par The first was an agenda for the two hundred and fourth ordinary session, item 9(c).
\par The second was a briefing note, four pages, from something called the Office of the President.
\par The third was a costed proposal for the discontinuation of the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 Galactic Health Support Programme}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
 with effect from the end of the current subscription year.
\par Beatrix Sloan read all three on the train from Gray's Inn and arrived at Marsham Street at twenty past eight in the morning without her coat, which she had left on the train.
\par "Neville," she said. "What is the Galactic Health Support Programme."
\par "I have no idea. Until this morning I did not know there was a galactic anything."
\par "It is forty-one signatories paying into a common fund," said Beatrix, "and the fund does exactly one thing, and it has done it since before the treaty was in English, and it is described in the founding instrument in a phrase I have now read nineteen tim
es." She put the paper down and read it out. "}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 The maintenance of full subscription upon local screens within the signatory volume.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 "
\par Fainrose, who had come in behind her and was standing very still in the doorway, said: "Say that again."
\par "The maintenance of full subscription upon local screens within the signatory volume."
\par Fainrose sat down on the edge of the table.
\par "They keep the walls written on," she said.
