\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 They got Priya Ramanathan down from Cheltenham on the Sunday and she brought a graduate student and four boxes and did not sleep.
\par "Right," she said on Monday morning. "Item seven. I want to be careful, because I have been up for thirty hours and I would rather be slow than wrong."
\par "Be slow," said Fainrose.
\par "A star does not burn because it is hot enough to burn. It is nowhere near hot enough." Ramanathan put a plot up. "Two protons in the core of a main-sequence star approach one another and are repelled, and classically they never touch, not at fifteen mill
ion kelvin, not at a hundred million. Fusion happens }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 only}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045  
by tunnelling. The whole of stellar power output is a barrier-penetration effect, and the penetration probability is exponential in the barrier, which means it is exponential in everything." She looked up. "Which means that stellar physics is the most sen
sitive amplifier of vacuum conditions that exists in nature, and nobody has ever needed to know that, because the vacuum has never changed."
\par Neville said, "Give me the number."
\par "Eleven parts in ten to the twenty-second." Ramanathan's mouth did something unpleasant. "In the biological estate, over six hours, that produced fourteen anomalies out of two hundred and nine, and it took Miss Pike three weeks of trace work to see it. In
 a stellar core, over six hours, with ten to the fifty-six participating nuclei and a Gamow factor in the exponent, that is not a small effect. That is a core running roughly two per cent fast for six hours."
\par "Which does what?"
\par "To a young star, nothing at all. It rings for a century and settles." Ramanathan turned the page. "To a core within a few thousand years of its own limit \emdash  a core that is already sitting on degeneracy pressure and waiting \emdash 
 two per cent for six hours is enough to take it over. Not enough to }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 cause}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
 a supernova. Enough to }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 advance one}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
. And that distinction will be the entire argument at the session and I want the department to be very clear about it before we go, because the President's brief has already found it."
