\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 The brief from the Office of the President ran to four pages and Neville came to think of it, afterwards, as the most accomplished document he had ever read.
\par It made three arguments and it did not raise its voice once.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 The first}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045  
was that the Programme could not demonstrate a benefit. Subscription maintenance is invisible when it works; there is no counterfactual galaxy to compare with; forty-one signatories had been paying for eleven thousand years for an absence of events. }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 The Programme's own performance indicator is that nothing occurred. The Office notes that nothing has also occurred in volumes where no subscription was maintained.}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045  This was untrue, but it was untrue in a way that required nine months of work to demonstrate, and the session was in three weeks.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 The second}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
 was that the Programme's costs fell disproportionately on the paying signatories while its benefits accrued to the unsubscribed volume. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
The Office does not consider it equitable that the responsible parties should indefinitely underwrite the untidiness of others.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 The third}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
 argument was the one that made Fainrose put the paper down and go and stand at the window.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
The Office draws the session's attention to the settled position that information within the signatory volume is conserved. The Office is advised that no process occurring at any screen destroys information, and that all apparent loss is a change of descr
iption rather than a change of content. The Office therefore finds it difficult to identify the harm which the Programme exists to prevent. In a unitary volume there is no such thing as damage. There is only re-encoding.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
\par And in a footnote:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 The Office is grateful to Professor M. Tegn\'e9r for his assistance in the preparation of this paragraph.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
