\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 Beatrix Sloan was called at four twenty, as counsel for a non-signatory observer with leave to be heard, and she had eleven minutes.
\par She used two of them on the facts and nine on the law.
\par "The Office's third argument," she said, "is that in a unitary volume there is no damage, only re-encoding. The Office's authority for that is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 complementarity}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 , and I want to state that doctrine fairly, because it is correct and because I intend to rely on it myself.
\par "Complementarity holds that where a screen is concerned, there are two accounts. There is the account of the party who remains outside, for whom the interior information is on the surface, and who sees nothing lost. And there is the account of the party w
ho goes in, for whom the interior is a place, and who sees no surface at all. Both accounts are consistent. Neither is incomplete. And \emdash  this is the part the Office has built its case on \emdash  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 no observer can hold both}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
. There is no vantage from which the two accounts can be compared, and so there is no contradiction, and so nothing has gone wrong.
\par "The Office says: since no one may compare the two accounts, no one has standing to allege a loss. My client's fourteen citizens are living in Peterhead and are also data on a rewritten screen, and these are the same thing described twice, and the Office 
invites the session to find that there is therefore nothing to remedy.
\par "I say the Office is thirty years out of date."
\par She turned a page.
\par "Because complementarity's protection has a condition, and the condition failed. To maintain both accounts, the interior partner must be fully correlated with the outgoing radiation }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 and}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045  with the interior remainder, at the same time. And it is a theorem \emdash 
 not a view, a theorem, and this session has already adopted it in the schedule to the instrument of the year before last \emdash  that this is impossible. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
Correlation is monogamous.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045  
A system maximally correlated with one partner cannot be correlated with a second at all. The two accounts the Office relies upon require the same correlation to be spent twice, and it cannot be spent twice, and so they are not two consistent descriptions
 of one event. They are two claims, and at most one of them is true.
\par "Which means the comparison the Office says is forbidden is not forbidden. It is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 decisive}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
. And where a rewrite of a screen requires the same correlation to be spent twice, the deficit is not an artefact of description. It is a physical loss, at a definite place, of a definite size, and it can be measured, and my client has measured it.
\par "S was two point four one. The ceiling for a settled record is two. The prediction for an intact one is two point eight. My client published that number in a Statement of Coherence in the year before last and was widely criticised for it, largely by me.

\par "The Office says there is no such thing as damage in a unitary volume. I say that unitarity guarantees that the information still exists. It does not guarantee that it exists }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 here}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
, and it does not guarantee that anyone in this room can get at it, and a conservation law is not a defence to a charge of taking. The Office has confused }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
the accounts balance}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045  with }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 nothing has happened}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 , and every institution I have ever audited has made exactly that error, and it has never once been an accident."
\par She sat down at four thirty-one.
\par There was a silence of some length.
\par Then the President of the Galactic Counsel leaned into his microphone and said:
\par "Very well spoken. Very impressive. But it's over. We're not paying."
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
