\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 Ramanathan telephoned from Cheltenham at eleven that night, and Neville took it in the hotel corridor.
\par "I've finished the bearing," she said. "Twelve degrees off the plane. I've been sitting on it for two days because I wanted the systematics right."
\par "Go on."
\par "It's a core-collapse event. Type II, ordinary in every respect, except for the timing." A pause, and paper. "Progenitor mass models put it eleven to fourteen thousand years early. And the light left it during a window that is consistent, to the limit of 
my resolution, with the fourteenth of March here."
\par Neville stood in the corridor with the telephone.
\par "Priya. It was six hours."
\par "It was six hours }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 here}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
," said Priya Ramanathan. "Nobody has ever suggested it was six hours only here. And I would like to say, on the record, before somebody in a good suit says it first, that the star did not explode because the vacuum dipped. It was always going to explode.
 It explodes eleven thousand years early, which is nothing, cosmically. Absolutely nothing." Her voice was perfectly steady. "There are two hundred and six cores in this arm within four thousand years of their limit, and I have the list, and the Programme
 has three months left."
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid13851045 
