\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 Dougbart Stadthof arrived on the Thursday, which was Mrs Kind's day, and the two of them got on so immediately and so loudly that Miss Pike had to move them out of the open plan.

\par He was sixty-three, bearded, in a jacket with a pencil in the breast pocket and rosin on the cuff, and he talked the way an organ sounds when the blower is on and nobody is playing yet \emdash  a constant low readiness that occasionally became music.

\par "Before anything," he said, "I want to be clear about what I am and am not. I am not a physicist. I am a man who tunes reed stops and translates poetry for fun, and everything I know about your subject I know because in nineteen seventy-six I was regulati
ng a Father Smith in a Fenland church and I noticed something about a fugue and I have not recovered."
\par Fainrose said, "Noticed what?"
\par "That a fugue is a machine that contains a description of itself, and that it can operate on that description, and that this is not a metaphor." He put a score on the table. "Bach. The canon that modulates up a tone and then does it again and then again, 
and after six repetitions you are back where you started, having risen the entire time. You cannot point to the place where it turns round, because it does not turn round. It goes up for ever and arrives home. There is a print by a Dutchman of two hands d
ra
wing one another which is the same object. There is a theorem by an Austrian which is the same object. Three men in three trades made the identical thing in the same century and none of them knew, and I have spent forty-seven years trying to say why, and 
the name I have given the attempt is the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 Eternal Golden Braid}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 
, and I am aware, Dr Fainrose, that a man who names his theory is usually a man who has not finished it."
\par "Is it finished?"
\par "No," said Stadthof cheerfully. "It is not even wrong yet. Appendices A to C are three hundred pages of a man in love. What I have brought that is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 usable}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366  is eleven pages, and I would rather we spent the day on those, because the rest is my hobby and this is apparently an emergency."
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 
