\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 Appendix D was four pages and it concerned Article 2 of the founding instrument, and it began with an anecdote.
\par "In nineteen forty-seven," said Stadthof, "the Austrian went to his citizenship hearing in New Jersey, having prepared for it in the manner of a logician, which is to say he had read the constitution of the country he was applying to join. He told his fri
ends beforehand that he had found an internal inconsistency in it \emdash 
 a chain of provisions which, followed correctly, permitted the lawful establishment of a dictatorship. His friends begged him not to raise it at the hearing. He very nearly did. The judge, being a sensible man, changed the subject.
\par "Now." He turned the page round. "Article 2 of your instrument. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 
The Office shall determine all questions as to the scope and application of this instrument, including questions as to the extent of the Office's own competence to so determine.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 "

\par Fainrose said, "That's a self-certification clause."
\par "It is more than that, it is the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 sentence}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 
," said Stadthof. "That clause makes the Counsel's instrument a formal system which contains a complete description of itself and the authority to reason about it. Which means it has all the Austrian's diseases and none of his humility. And in particular 
it means that somewhere in that instrument there is a motion which the Counsel can neither pass nor reject, and I have written it out, and it is on page four, and I should say that I wrote it as a joke in April."
\par Beatrix read page four.
\par Then she read it again.
\par Then she went out of the room and did not come back for fifty minutes, and when she did she had her sleeves up.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 
