{\*\pnseclvl7\pnlcrm\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang {\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl8\pnlcltr\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang {\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl9\pnlcrm\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang {\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}\pard\plain \ltrpar
\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 
The motion, as eventually laid before the two hundred and sixth session, ran to a single sentence, and Neville came to think of it as the second most accomplished document he had ever read.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 That the Office lacks competence to determine any question upon which the Office's own competence is the question at issue; and that this motion is such a question.}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 
\par "Look at what it does," said Beatrix, at half past nine that night, with the whole department round the table and Stadthof visibly delighted with himself. "If the Office rules the motion out of order, it has determined a question upon which its own compet
ence was at issue \emdash  which is the very thing the motion says it may not do. So its ruling has no standing, and the motion survives.
\par "If the Office rules the motion in order and the session rejects it, then the session has affirmed that the Office }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 does}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366  
have that competence, in a vote whose validity depends on the Office having had competence to put it to them. The rejection assumes what it decides. It is circular, and it is void on its face, and I will bring that in any forum in the galaxy.
\par "And if the Office does nothing at all, the motion is pending. And pending, under Article 9, suspends the operation of any decision of the session which depends on the disputed competence."
\par Neville said, quietly, "Item nine C."
\par "Item nine C," said Beatrix. "The discontinuation of the Galactic Health Support Programme was a decision of the session taken on the Office's ruling as to scope. It depends on the disputed competence. It cannot take effect while the question is pending."
 She sat back. "And the question cannot be decided. Not by them. Not ever. The Austrian's point is that there is no move available inside the system."
\par "So we've stopped it," said Miss Pike.
\par "We have }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 frozen}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366  
it," said Beatrix. "Which is not the same thing and I want that on the record. I have not saved the Programme. I have put it in a state that cannot be resolved by the body with authority over it, which \emdash  Neville, you will forgive me \emdash 
 is precisely the crime we spent Book One prosecuting."
\par There was a rather long silence.
\par Fainrose said, "Yes. It is."
\par "I know."
\par "Do it anyway."
\par "I intend to," said Beatrix Sloan. "I want it minuted that I know what it is, that is all. Somebody in this room ought to be in the habit."
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 
