Mrs Kind had spent the afternoon on the winding-up schedule, because that was the sort of thing she was for, and she raised her hand at ten to ten in the manner of a person who has read the annex nobody else has reached.
\par "Before everyone celebrates," she said. "Assets."
\par "Sorry?"
\par "The motion in Vienna provided that on discontinuation the Programme's assets be realised and its records lodged with the Office of the President." She had it flagged. "I have been trying since Tuesday to work out what a subscription-maintenance body owns
. It has no vessels. It has eleven leased premises and some instruments and a pension liability. Its realisable value is essentially nil."
\par "Then what's the concern?"
\par "The }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 records}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 
," said Mrs Kind. "Mr Wren, what does a body that spends eleven thousand years topping up slack screens necessarily possess?"
\par Neville understood it about a second before she said it, and had to sit down.
\par "A map," he said.
\par "A complete, current, galaxy-wide register of every under-subscribed screen in the signatory volume," said Mrs Kind. "Every thin place. Every wall with a gap in it. Sorted, one presumes, by how slack, because that is how you would sequence the maintenance
 rounds." She closed the folder. "It is the only document of its kind in existence, it took eleven thousand years to compile, it cannot be reconstructed by anybody in under a millennium, and clause 14 lodges it with the Office of the President in the even
t of a discontinuation which, thanks to Ms Sloan, will now never technically occur."
\par Beatrix said, "Then the lodgement is suspended too."
\par "Is it?" said Mrs Kind. "Clause 14 isn't a decision of the session. It's a standing provision of the instrument, triggered by the resolution's }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 passage}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 , not its coming into effect. I have booked three hundred and eleven group tours on contracts drafted like that. The cancellation is suspended. The handover isn't."
\par Nobody spoke.
\par "When," said Fainrose.
\par "The papers went across on the eleventh of June," said Mrs Kind.
