Any consistent formal system able to express arithmetic contains true statements it cannot prove, and cannot be repaired by adding them.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\insrsid14645859\charrsid5398366 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}No such system can prove its own consistency; self-certification carries no information.
