\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 Priya Ramanathan came in at four with the 4C radiation curve, because she had been promised ten minutes and had waited three hours for them.
\par "Briefly," she said. "I've dated the crossover on Four C. For the first part of its evaporation the radiation carried essentially nothing \emdash 
 the correlations were all still inside. Then it turned over, and after that every quantum leaving carried structure
, and the outside began to hold more of the record than the inside did. It rises and then it falls, and the peak is the moment the account changes hands."
\par "When?" said Fainrose.
\par "Four C crossed over in nineteen sixty-one," said Ramanathan.
\par Mrs Kind looked up from the leasehold schedule.
\par "Nineteen sixty-one," she said, "is the year the clerk filed the treaty instrument under the wrong word."
\par Nobody was quite prepared to say anything about that, then or later, and Neville noted it in the margin and drew a box round it and did not write a conclusion.
