\ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 undecidable}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 .
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 Equilibrium, and why the Programme was structurally doomed.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384  Nash's 1950 result \emdash 
 his doctoral thesis ran twenty-seven pages \emdash  established that every finite non-cooperative game has at least one point at which no player can improve by unilaterally changing strategy. For a public-good game with diffuse benefit and s
pecific cost, non-contribution strictly dominates: whatever the others do, an individual member does better by withholding. The unique equilibrium is universal defection, and no malice is required to reach it. Nash regarded the game theory as minor; his o
wn estimate of his best work was the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 embedding theorems}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384  (1954\endash 
56), which prove that any Riemannian manifold admits an isometric embedding into a Euclidean space of sufficient dimension \emdash  a curved intrinsic description is always available as a plain extrinsic one, which is why the chapter has him glance at the
 holography board.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 Why cooperation nevertheless persists.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384  
Indefinitely repeated play with observable defection can stabilise cooperation without altruism, through the shadow of future punishment. This requires monitoring and enforcement. The chapter's premise is that the Counsel had neither, and that the founder
s therefore solved the problem in a way that needs neither.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 Nonlocal games.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384  
A nonlocal game is Bell's theorem restated operationally: two separated players receive random inputs from a referee, return outputs, and win according to a predicate on all four values. They may pre-agree any strategy and share unlimited classical random
ness, but cannot communicate after inputs are issued.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls11\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid5709733 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 The }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 CHSH game}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384  has classical optimum 75%. With a shared maximally entangled pair, the optimum rises to }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 
\ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs20\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 \\cos^2(\\pi/8) \\approx 85.4\\%}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 , corresponding to Tsirelson's bound }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f2\fs20\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 2\\sqrt\{2\} \\approx 2.828}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384  against the classical 2.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}The }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 Mermin\endash 
Peres magic square game}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384  is starker: classical play cannot exceed 8/9, while an entangled strategy wins with probability 1.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 
Crucially, entanglement transmits no information \emdash  the local marginals are unchanged and no signalling is possible \emdash 
 yet it enables coordination provably unachievable by any prior agreement. That combination is precisely what a self-enforcing compact need
s: performance that cannot be faked because the ceiling on faking is a theorem rather than a standard. This is also the real basis of device-independent cryptography and randomness certification, where security rests on observed violation of a classical b
ound rather than on trust in hardware.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 The monogamy cap is genuine.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 
 Because maximal entanglement is monogamous (Book One, Chapter Fifteen), a fixed store of correlation cannot underwrite an unbounded membership. Distributing it across many parties yields weak pairwise correlation that fails to violate the classical bound
 reliably, and the scheme degrades into mutual assertion. The membership limit is arithmetic, not policy \emdash  and the chapter is deliberate in refusing to make the choice of the nine anything other than a moral injury.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 Undecidability, and why it lands here.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384  In 2020 Ji, Natarajan, Vidick, Wright and Yuen proved }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 MIP* = RE}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 
: the class of problems decidable by interactive proofs with entangled provers is exactly the recursively enumerable sets. The corollary is that approximating the entangled value of a nonlocal game is as hard as the halting problem, and therefore undecida
ble \emdash  one can write down a finite game whose optimal score no algorithm computes. The same result settled }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 Tsirelson's problem}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384  negatively (the finite-dimensional and commuting-operator values of games differ) and thereby refuted the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 
Connes embedding conjecture}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 
 in operator algebras. It also implies that for some games the achievable score strictly improves as the shared entangled system is enlarged, without ever attaining its limit: no finite amount of correlation suffices, and the shortfall is not computably b
ounded.
\par This is Chapter Six's theorem returning at the level of physical strategy rather than formal proof, and it is the chapter's plot engine: a protocol that adjudicates by play is only safe if the game is fixed in advance. Grant any party the right to propose
 the game and you have granted the right to hang the protocol permanently.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 The Page curve, in passing.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384  Ramanathan's crossover is Page's 1993 result: t
he entanglement entropy of radiation from an evaporating black hole rises while the interior still holds the record, peaks at the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 Page time}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384  when roughly half the entropy has been emitted, and thereafter falls as the outside becomes the more complete description. Recovering that curve from gravity \emdash 
 via replica wormholes and entanglement islands, from 2019 onward \emdash  is the strongest current evi
dence that evaporation is unitary. It matters here because the Page time is the moment custody changes hands, which the series has been treating as a legal event since Book One.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs27 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs27\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 
