Nash equilibrium: in a public-good game with diffuse benefits, withholding dominates, and universal defection is the stable point without any villain.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}Repeated play can sustain cooperation, but only with monitoring and enforcement \emdash 
 neither of which the Counsel possesses.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
Nonlocal games recast Bell's theorem: CHSH caps classical play at 75% versus 85.4% with entanglement, and the magic square game at 8/9 versus certainty.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
Entanglement enables coordination without communication, which is why it can certify compliance without inspectors or trust.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}Monogamy of entanglement imposes a hard limit on how many parties a fixed correlation store can bind.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
MIP* = RE: the value of a nonlocal game is undecidable, larger entangled systems can help without limit, and Tsirelson's problem and the Connes embedding conjecture fell with it.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\insrsid14645859\charrsid8355384 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}The Page curve marks the point at which the outside becomes the more complete description of an evaporating object.

