\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 "Very well," said Fainrose, "and now the part that concerns my hundred and twelve days, because you did not come from Cambridge to review a sixty-year-old essay."
\par "No." Eugenius put a single sheet on the table. "I came because of paragraph 9 of Ms Sloan's draft protocol, which reads: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 
a party which has not maintained held correlations cannot attain a score above the classical ceiling, the ceiling being a theorem and not a standard.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 "
\par "That's Nashville's point and it's correct."
\par "It is correct }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 within the formalism}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 ," said Viktor Eugenius. "And a theorem constrains a }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 model}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 
. It does not constrain a world. It constrains the world only to the exact extent that the world is faithfully described by the framework in which the theorem was proved, and }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 that}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 
 is not a theorem. That is an empirical claim, with a domain of validity, like every other empirical claim, and it has never once been tested in the regime you are now operating in."
\par Beatrix said, "Say the regime."
\par "Every experiment that has ever confirmed your ceiling \emdash  and there are thousands, and they are excellent, and I believe every one of them \emdash  was performed against a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 fixed background}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 
. The vacuum stayed where it was. Nobody had lowered the price of nothing by eleven parts in ten to the twenty-second while the apparatus was running." He tapped the sheet. "You have discovered that the background is an }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 editable quantity}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 
. And you have then gone on to build an enforcement mechanism whose entire security rests on a bound derived by assuming it is not."
\par There was a silence of the specific kind that Neville had learned to recognise as the sound of a department realising it had been holding something upside down.
\par "Give me the number," said Fainrose. "You have one."
\par "I have three." Eugenius held up a hand. "Your classical ceiling is two. Your quantum ceiling \emdash  the one Ms Sloan's protocol relies upon \emdash 
 is two point eight two eight, and everybody in this room thinks of that as the ceiling imposed by the universe.
\par "It is not. The ceiling imposed by }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 relativity alone}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496  \emdash 
 by the requirement that no correlation can be used to send a signal, which is the only thing we know from principle rather than from formalism \emdash  is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 four}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 ."
\par Nobody spoke.
\par "There is a perfectly consistent hypothetical device, in the literature since nineteen ninety-four, which scores four. It transmits no information. It violates no relativity. It cannot be used to signal. It simply achieves correlations stronger than quant
um mechanics permits, and nothing in the structure of spacetime forbids it. Quantum theory forbids it, which is a very different statement." He sat back. "There is a beautiful argument that the reason we live at two point eight two eight and not four has 
to do with the amount of information one party can extract about another's data \emdash  an axiom about communication rather than about mechanics. It is elegant and I believe it. But it is an }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 axiom}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 
, and axioms are things one has adopted, and I have spent an unpleasant month asking myself what would happen to that axiom in a volume where somebody is rewriting screens, and I do not know, and neither does anybody, and Ms Sloan has drafted a protocol w
hich reads a high score as proof of good standing."
\par Beatrix Sloan said, very quietly, "Then a cheat scores above the quantum bound."
\par "A cheat with a vacuum budget and no held correlations at all," said Eugenius, "scores three poi
nt four, and your protocol certifies him as the most compliant member of the nine, and every honest party sitting at two point eight is marked down as a laggard. You have not built a system that is impossible to fake. You have built one where the }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 only}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 
 way to fake it is to be the one entity in the galaxy who has been editing screens, and where the fake presents as excellence."
