\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 The rest of the day was operational, and Neville wrote the operational parts up in the minute rather than the notebook, except for three items.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 Item one: Miss Pike's proposal.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 
 She had worked out where to get correlation to refill the eleven rooms, and it was the least comfortable place available.
\par "Four C crossed over in nineteen sixty-one," she said. "Priya's curve. Before that the radiation carried nothing. After that, every quantum leaving carries structure, and the outside holds more of the record than the inside does. Which means Four C has be
en }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 emitting usable correlation}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496  
for sixty-five years, and we have been treating the entire volume as a crime scene and a mausoleum and we have never once put a collector on it."
\par Fainrose said, "You want to harvest the horizon."
\par "I want to harvest the horizon of the object we recovered three hundred and eight people from," said Miss Pike, "and I have written down all four of the reasons that is monstrous, and I have also written down what happens to a hundred and ninety-five thin
 records in this country alone if the walls go slack in February, and I would like the department to decide rather than me."
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 Item two: van Casteel's lease.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496  
He came up from Cumbria on the Thursday with a photocopy from a county record office and put it on the table without sitting down.
\par "My mineshaft," he said. "I have worked in it for nineteen years and my employer leased it in nineteen sixty-three from a company in Kendal. That company took an underlease in eighteen ninety. The head lease is dated fourteen hundred and eleven and the le
ssee is not named, and the covenant \emdash  the one covenant, gentlemen, on the entire instrument, in Latin, in a hand I had to pay a man in Carlisle to read \emdash  is that the demised chamber }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 shall be kept still, and dark, and undisturbed, and its contents shall not be counted}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 ."
\par Fainrose said, "Shall not be counted."
\par "Shall not be counted," said Hendrik van Casteel. "I have spent nineteen years in that chamber measuring the force between two plates to eleven significant figures, and I would like somebody in this building to tell me whether I have been the tenant or th
e breach."
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 Item three: the Vienna premises.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 
 Mrs Kind found it at ten past six and made everybody wait while she read it twice.
\par "Two Vienna leases," she said. "The first is the registry. Rates, cleaner, a strong room, all completely ordinary, and the map went into it on the eleventh of June.
\par "The second is a single room on the fourth floor of a building off the Ringstrasse and it has been leased continuously since the founding, and it has no telephone, no instruments, no strong room, and no fixtures beyond a table and two chairs, and the serv
ice charge is nil, and the purpose clause reads: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 for the accommodation of an unaffiliated observer.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 "
\par Neville said, "Meaning what?"
\par "Meaning it is deliberately empty," said Mrs Kind. "Eleven thousand years, forty-one signatories, and a room maintained at the founders' expense for somebody who belongs to none of them, to come and look, and to say whether what the Counsel had done was a
 thing anybody needed."
\par Stadthof put down his tea.
\par "Somebody outside has to look," he said, "and somebody inside has to be asked."
\par "How many times has it been used?" said Beatrix.
\par Mrs Kind checked the occupancy schedule, which was one page, and had eleven thousand years on it, and was very nearly blank.
\par "Twice," she said.
