\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 Neville wrote, at midnight:
\par Effectiveness of mathematics: mostly a selection effect.\line We call the amenable part physics. The rest we call immature.\line We built the tool out of the world. 99% of the arrows miss and we frame the eleven.
\par Then:
\par A theorem constrains a model, not a world.\line The bound holds only where the framework holds. That is empirical.\line Every test was against a fixed background. Ours is not fixed.
\par Then, underlined:
\par Classical 2. Quantum 2.828. No-signalling allows 4.\line Superquantum breaks no relativity. Only our formalism.\line A cheat with a vacuum budget scores 3.4 and reads as our best member.\line Honest parties get marked down. Rewrite paragraph 9.
\par Then:
\par Priya's answer, and I think it is the real one:\line Decoherence is a sieve. Pointer states are the ones with short descriptions.\line Mathematics works because we live downstream of a filter that removed everything it couldn't handle.\line 
The sieve runs on the environment. The environment is the screens.\line Full subscription buys classicality. That is what the line item was.
\par Then:
\par Failure will not look like physics breaking.\line It will look like things being slightly less predictable, unrecorded, for a century, then all at once.
\par Then:
\par Pike: harvest 4C's horizon. She wrote down the four reasons it's monstrous. So should we. Decide it as a department. Not her.\line 
Van Casteel: head lease 1411. Kept still, dark, undisturbed. Contents shall not be counted. He has counted them to eleven figures for nineteen years.
\par And last:
\par Vienna, fourth floor. A table and two chairs. Nil service charge.\line For the accommodation of an unaffiliated observer.\line Eleven thousand years.\line Used twice.
