ed}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 ited vacuum nobody has established.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 Decoherence and einselection, which is the chapter's answer.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 
 A quantum system is never isolated; its environment continuously interacts with it, and the resulting entanglement destroys interference between most superpositions with extraordinary speed \emdash  for a dust grain in ambient sunlight, on the order of }
{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs20\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 10^\{-20\}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496  
seconds. The surviving states are not arbitrary. The interaction picks out a preferred basis: those states that are stable under monitoring and are copied redundantly into the environment rather than scrambled. Zurek named this }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 einselection}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496  (environment-induced superselection), and the selected states are }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 pointer states}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496  \emdash  position, charge, definite instrument readings.
\par The consequence Ramanathan draws is a serious position and not merely a plot device. Pointer states are precisely those with robust, local, redundantly recordable \emdash  and therefore compressible and predictable \emdash  descriptions. }{\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 Quantum Darwinism}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496  
makes this explicit: what counts as objective classical reality is the small subset of information that many independent fragments of the environment agree upon. If the classical world is the output of such a sieve, then the effectiveness of mathematics i
s less miraculous, because everything mathematics could not have handled was removed before it reached the level at which we describe anything. Mathematics is effective on the residue, and the residue is defined by being describable.
\par In this book's fiction, that sieve runs on the screens, and full subscription is what continuous environmental monitoring looks like from inside. That converts the Programme's cancelled line item from a safety measure into the purchase of }{\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 lawfulness itself}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496  \emdash 
 and it makes Eugenius's closing warning the correct one, since a weakening sieve does not present as physics failing but as a slow, unrecorded loss of predictability in domains nobody audits.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496 The Page-time harvest.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid8469496  
Miss Pike's proposal rests on Chapter Seven's crossover: after the Page time, the emitted radiation carries more of the record than the interior, so correlations extracted from it are not noise but structure. Whether it is defensible to harvest correlatio
n from the horizon of an object from which three hundred and eight people were recovered is not a physics question, and the chapter is deliberate in refusing to let one analyst decide it.
