\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 He did the physics briskly, with no chalk, sitting still.
\par "Start with the equations everybody agrees about. Newton's, Maxwell's, the Schr\'f6dinger equation, general relativity. Every one of them is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 symmetric under reversal}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 . Run the film backwards and you get another perfectly lawful film. There is nothing in the fundamental description that distinguishes forward from back \emdash 
 the weak interaction has a small asymmetry, and it is far too small and quite the wrong shape to account for anything you experience.
\par "So where does your Tuesday come from? Not from the laws. The only asymmetry anywhere in physics is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 thermodynamic}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 : entropy is higher in one direction. And Boltzmann showed that this is not a law but a matter of counting \emdash 
 there are overwhelmingly more disordered arrangements than ordered ones, so a system found in an ordered arrangement will almost certainly be found less ordered later. Fine. But the argument is symmetric. The same counting says the system was }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 also}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635  almost certainly less ordered }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 earlier}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 , which is flatly contrary to every record you possess.
\par "The only way anybody has ever got out of this is to assume it. You put in, by hand, the statement that the universe began in a state of extraordinarily low entropy \emdash  the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 Past Hypothesis}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635  \emdash 
 and everything follows: the arrow, memory, causation, the fact that you remember March and not February of next year. The special-ness required is grotesque. One estimate puts the initial state as one arrangement in ten to the power ten to the power a h
undred and twenty-three. It is the largest unexplained number in science and we treat it as a boundary condition, which is what physicists say when they mean }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
we have agreed not to ask}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 ."
\par Stadthof said, happily, "So there is no time and also the arrow is smuggled in."
\par "Worse," said Barbarian. "Look at general relativity properly and time does not appear as a parameter at all. Write the theory in Hamiltonian form and you do not get an equation of the form }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 the state changes thus per second}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 . You get a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
constraint}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 : the total is zero. Quantise it and you get the Wheeler\endash DeWitt equation, }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs20\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
\\hat\{H\}\\Psi = 0}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 , and the wavefunction of the universe simply }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 is}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
. Stationary. No evolution. No parameter to evolve along. The fundamental description of the whole thing contains no clock, and this is not a fringe view, it is what the equation says, and the field has spent sixty years calling it the problem of time as 
though the equation had made an error.
\par "My position \emdash  and here I am the crank, and I am content to be \emdash 
 is that there is no error. There is a vast, static space of possible configurations of everything: every arrangement of every relative distance, all at once, none of them 'now'. Some of those configurations are extraordinarily special. They contain }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 structures which are consistent with each other as records of other configurations}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
. A rock with strata. A photograph. A brain holding what it calls a memory. A green notebook with a date at the top." He looked at Neville. "I call those time capsules. And the experience of time, and the sense of having come from somewhere, is what it is
 like to be a configuration of that kind. Not a journey. A property.
\par "And there is a respectable mechanism, which is not mine, and which I want on the record because it keeps me out of the mystics' tent. Take a static, globally stationary state. Divide it into a small subsystem you call a clock and the rest you call the wo
rld. Then ask, not what the world is doing at time t, but what the world's state is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 conditional on the clock reading t}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 . That conditional state obeys the ordinary Schr\'f6
dinger equation, exactly. Time is not the container. It is the correlation between the clock and everything else, and it has been simulated with photons, and it works."
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
