\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 "Right," said Fainrose. "Now do the damage. You said this matters to the protocol."
\par "It gutters the protocol," said Barbarian, "and I am sorry, because I read the draft on the train and it is a beautiful piece of work.
\par "Paragraph 11. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 A party shall demonstrate maintained subscription by achieving the quantum score at intervals not exceeding one century.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635  Ms Sloan, that clause presupposes that there is a fact about what happened between the intervals. It does not measure maintenance. It measures a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 configuration}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 , twice, and infers a history connecting them.
\par "But on any account of time that survives the Wheeler\endash DeWitt equation, and on plenty that do not, the history is not an extra thing sitting behind the records. The history }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 is}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635  
the mutual consistency of the records. Which means that what you actually test is whether a party can present a configuration containing structures consistent with having maintained subscription for a hundred years." He let that sit. "And that is a differ
ent requirement, and it is one that can in principle be met by a party who has not maintained anything at all and has instead }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 built the records}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 ."
\par Miss Pike said, very quietly, "Column B."
\par "I beg your pardon?"
\par "There was a column," said Miss Pike. "In the year before last. I fabricated it in four minutes because the directive required a certainty I did not have, and I confessed inside the hour, and it is in the schedule to the Act with my name on it." She had g
one slightly grey again. "Mr Barbarian, you have just described what I did, at the scale of a galaxy."
\par "Then you are the only person in this room who has already run the experiment," said Szmulek Barbarian, "and I should very much like to know what it cost you, because that is the thing I have never been able to calculate."
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
