\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
It cost Ramanathan and Fainrose and Miss Pike eleven hours, and they came back at nine that night with the answer, and it was the best thing the department produced in the whole of that year.
\par "He's right about the requirement," said Ramanathan, "and he's wrong about the practicality, and the reason is Chapter Nine."
\par "Say it properly," said Fainrose.
\par "A forged past is not one record. It cannot be." Ramanathan put it up. "A single document proving a century of compliance is worth nothing, and everybody knows it's worth nothing, which is why nobody has ever tried. To be }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 believed}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 , a history has to be redundant \emdash 
 written into a large number of independent places that were never coordinated. That is what makes a fact hard to argue with, and it is the only thing that does.
\par "So a fabricated century does not require one lie. It requires }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs20\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 R}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
 independent, mutually consistent copies, held by parties who have not communicated, with no correlations between them beyond the ones a genuine history would have produced. And copies cost }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 surface capacity}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
. Every record written into the environment consumes area on a screen, at four Planck areas a bit, and there is no discount for the record being false."
\par Beatrix said, slowly, "So forgery has a price."
\par "Forgery has a price and it is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 the same price as the truth}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
, plus the coordination overhead of making the copies look uncoordinated, which is the expensive part." Ramanathan almost smiled. "Mr Barbarian, that is what Column B cost. It cost Miss Pike four minutes to write and it was detectable in under an hour, be
cause she produced one copy and the world had ten to the eleven copies of something else, and one against ten to the eleven is not a dispute, it is arithmetic.
\par "To forge a century of subscription across nine signatories, at a redundancy sufficient to survive an audit, you would need to write approximately as much onto the screens as maintaining it would have written. And here is the part I like. }{\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 You cannot do that on a slack screen.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
 A slack screen is precisely a screen without spare capacity to write on, because slackness }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 is}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635  
the absence of writing. So the only entity that can forge the record is an entity with a surplus of surface capacity, and the only way to get a surplus is to have cleared some, and clearing is visible as a vacuum excursion, and we have four instruments th
at see those to eleven parts in ten to the twenty-second."
\par Fainrose said, "Rewrite paragraph 11. Don't test the score. Test the redundancy."
\par "Test the redundancy," said Ramanathan, "and require that the copies be lodged with parties who can be shown not to hold copies in common, which is Mrs Kind's clause from last week, which means the protocol needs the Vienna room to work and not merely as 
a courtesy."
\par Szmulek Barbarian sat for a while with his hands on the table.
\par "Thirty-one years," he said. "I have been telling people that there is no time and that history is nothing but the consistency of records, and every single one of them has heard it as a licence \emdash  as though I were saying the past is }{\rtlch\fcs1 
\ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 cheap}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
. And a civil servant's analyst has just told me, with a number, that it is exactly as expensive as it appears to be, and that this is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 why}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635  it is real." He looked up. "I would like that in writing as well, please. Mr van Casteel has a receipt. I should like a receipt."
