\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 The notebooks.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
 Van Casteel's eleven notebooks went to a numerical analyst on secondment and to Miss Pike, and the result came back on the Friday, and Miss Pike would not present it standing up.
\par "The store in the Cumbrian chamber has been decaying since at least two thousand and seven, which is when Hendrik started measuring," she said. "The decay is not exponential. It is exponential with steps."
\par "Steps how?"
\par "There are seven intervals in nineteen years \emdash  averaging about eleven months each, irregularly spaced \emdash  during which the decay does not merely slow. It }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 reverses
}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
." She put the plot on the table. "Something was putting correlation back into that chamber. Seven times. Between two thousand and eight and two thousand and twenty-two. And there are no instruments in the eleven rooms and no Programme field team has visi
ted Cumbria since nineteen sixty-three, and the service charge for replenishment has not been drawn on the common fund since\emdash " she checked, unnecessarily \emdash  "nineteen sixty-one."
\par Fainrose said, "Then who has been paying it?"
\par Nobody wanted to say it, so Mrs Kind did, because Mrs Kind had spent twenty-two years telling people things about their arrangements that they had not wished to hear.
\par "Somebody who acquires correlation as a by-product of eating," she said, "and who has told us to our faces that he wants the ledger preserved, and who has been standing in our lobby waiting to be asked, and who has gone from comfortable to visibly thin in
 the eleven months since something stopped him feeding."
\par "Seven top-ups," said Neville. "Fourteen years. Out of his own \emdash  what would you even call it."
\par "Dinner," said Mrs Kind.
