\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 Neville wrote, at one in the morning:
\par The fundamental equations run both ways. The weak asymmetry is the wrong size and shape.\line The only arrow is entropy, and Boltzmann's counting works in both directions.\line 
So the past is assumed, by hand. 1 in 10^10^123. We call it a boundary condition.\line That is what a physicist says when he means we have agreed not to ask.
\par Then:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af51 \ltrch\fcs0 \f51\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 Wheeler-DeWitt: H\'d8 = 0. No parameter. The state simply is.\line Time may be the correlation between a clock and everything else.\line }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 Barbarian's capsules: configurations containing structures consistent as records of one another.\line A rock with strata. A photograph. This notebook.
\par Then, underlined twice:
\par Paragraph 11 does not test maintenance. It tests a configuration and infers a history.\line A forged century needs R independent copies. Copies cost area. Four Planck areas a bit.\line 
Forgery costs the same as the truth, plus the cost of making the copies look uncoordinated.\line And it cannot be done on a slack screen, because slack IS the absence of writing.\line Test the redundancy, not the score.
\par Then, Pike:
\par Column B cost four minutes and was detectable in one hour.\line One copy against 10^11. Not a dispute. Arithmetic.\line She has run the experiment. She should stop apologising for it. I should tell her that.
\par Then:
\par Seven reversals. 2008-2022. ~11 months each.\line The replenishment line has been dead since 1961.\line He has been paying the service charge out of his dinner and calling it a larder.
\par Then, Stephanie to the nine:
\par I will not certify direction.\line A weakening arrow does not look like time reversing.\line It looks like archives becoming ambiguous about which entry came first.\line It looks like two parties both sincerely remembering being the one who was owed.

\par And last:
\par Nashville: it does not matter why he did it. That is what an outsider is for.
\par His question, which I cannot answer:\line if an outsider's certificate is good, may he still require an invitation?\line He did not ask it as philosophy.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs36 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs36\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
