\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 arrow of time}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 , the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
Past Hypothesis}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 , and the timeless reading of quantum gravity that Barbour has argued for since the 1980s.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 The laws do not distinguish the directions.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635  Newtonian mechanics, Maxwell's equations, the Schr\'f6
dinger equation and general relativity are all invariant under time reversal (strictly, under CPT). The weak interaction exhibits genuine T-violation, but it is minute and structurally unrelated to the th
ermodynamic asymmetry we experience. Nothing in the fundamental dynamics singles out a future.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 Boltzmann and Loschmidt.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635  
The observed asymmetry is thermodynamic: entropy increases. Boltzmann's statistical account explains why \emdash 
 there are vastly more high-entropy microstates than low-entropy ones, so a system in an atypical state will very probably be found in a more typical one later. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
Loschmidt's objection}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635  is that the argument is time-symmetric: the same reasoning applied backwards concludes the system was probably }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 also}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635  
higher-entropy earlier, contradicting every record. The statistical argument, taken alone, predicts that the past was as disordered as the future.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 The Past Hypothesis.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635  
The standard repair is to posit as a separate postulate that the universe began in an extremely low-entropy state. Everything else \emdash  the second law, memory, causation, the asymmetry of records \emdash 
 follows from that boundary condition plus ordinary dynamics. The required specialness is extraordinary: Penrose's estimate, based on the Weyl curvature of the initial state, is roughly one part in }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f2\fs20\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 10^\{10^\{123\}\}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 . No accepted explanation exists. Without the postulate, one confronts the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 Boltzmann brain}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635  
problem, in which observers with false memories arising from random fluctuations vastly outnumber those with genuine low-entropy pasts \emdash  which is a reductio, not a theory.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 Time in general relativity, and its absence.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 
 In canonical form, general relativity does not evolve a state along an external time. Reparametrisation invariance produces the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 Hamiltonian constraint}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 , and quantisation yields the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 Wheeler\endash DeWitt equation}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid6510635 :
