\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743 The Fourth Concordance}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743  
was the blow, and it landed on the Friday, and it did not come from the Office at all. It came in a message from the Concordance itself, transmitted apologetically through the registry, and it was signed by the delegate who had twice spoken in the minutes
.
\par The Concordance had maintained subscription across its own volume for four hundred years before accession. It had said so in Vienna and been thanked and minuted. Under the old paragraph 11 that had been a matter of assertion and standing. Under the new pa
ragraph 11 it was a matter of lodged, independent, uncoordinated copies.
\par And the Concordance had them. It had kept four hundred years of records with exemplary care, in the medium its people had used for such things since before their accession, which was }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743 correlation with a nearby stellar object}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743  \emdash 
 the records held not as marks on a surface but as correlations between their instruments and a star, replenished each generation, requiring the star's continued state to decode.
\par The star was at twelve degrees off the plane.
\par "Say it plainly," said Fainrose, when the room had been quiet for long enough.
\par "Their archive was keyed to the progenitor," said Ramanathan. "It went core-collapse eleven to fourteen thousand years early, in a window consistent with the fourteenth of March. Everything they hold is now undecodable. Not lost. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743 Unreadable.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743 
 They have four hundred years of perfectly genuine, perfectly redundant compliance records and no key, and there is no key anywhere, because the key was a star and the star is a remnant."
\par Miss Pike said, "Then under our own clause\emdash "
\par "Under our own clause, the Fourth Concordance cannot demonstrate redundancy," said Beatrix Sloan, "and is therefore not admissible among the nine, and the Office of the President has already filed a motion to that effect, dated Wednesday, which is two day
s before the Concordance told us."
\par "They knew first."
\par "They have the map," said Mrs Kind.
\par Neville said, "Do we have a way out?"
\par "There is one and it is disgusting," said Beatrix. "The Concordance's copies exist. They are simply not decodable by us. But redundancy, as Dr Ramanathan defines it, is a count of independent fragments carrying the record \emdash 
 and the definition does not require that }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743 we}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743 
 can read them. It requires that they be there and be independent."
\par "Then we amend the clause to accept unreadable copies."
\par "And the moment we do, every fabricated archive in the galaxy is admissible on the grounds that its copies are merely awaiting a key," said Beatrix. "Which is the whole of the protection we bought from Mr Barbarian's objection. Neville, I want you to unde
rstand the shape of it. The only test that defeats a forged past is one that requires the copies to be readable. And the only member with four hundred genuine years cannot produce a readable copy, because the entity we are trying to restrain destroyed the
 key eleven thousand years early, in an event which is item seven of Annex C, which is the thing the Programme existed to prevent."
\par Szmulek Barbarian, who had been in the corner all afternoon and had said nothing, said:
\par "Then the Concordance is a rock whose strata are intact and whose light is gone. It is a time capsule that no longer capsules." He looked up. "I have spent thirty-one years saying that a past is nothing but the consistency of records, and I have been tell
ing you for three weeks that this makes the past expensive and therefore real. And here is a party whose records are entirely consistent and entirely mute, and I find I do not know whether they have a past or not, and I am ashamed of how interesting I fin
d that."
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743 
