gled in as the requirement of carbon-based observers specifically.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743 The chapter's actual argument, which is the one worth taking away.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743 
 The Office's move is not a physics error but a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743 tense error}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743 
, and it generalises well beyond fiction. Anthropic reasoning constrains what can be inferred from the fact of our existence: it establishes a lower bound on the past's permissiveness, and nothing more. It cannot certify that conditions were good, only th
at they were survivable \emdash 
 and by construction it can be invoked by any survivor of any severity of harm short of extinction. Nor does it carry forward: survival to the present is logically consistent with an arbitrarily severe change beginning immediately a
fterwards, because the selection effect operates on observations already made. A statement about the past presented in the tense of a guarantee is the specific abuse, and dating it is the answer.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743 Where it collides with Chapter Nine.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743 
 The Fourth Concordance's predicament follows strictly from the redundancy criterion. Redundancy counts independent environmental fragments carrying a record; the records exist and are independent, but their }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743 decoding key}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14645859\charrsid12780743  \emdash  the state of a stellar object used as the correlation reference \emdash 
 no longer exists. This is a real property of physical archives: information stored as correlation with an external system is recoverable only while that system's state persists, which is 
why practical archiving prefers redundant local encoding to correlation with a single reference. And it sharpens the dilemma the department created for itself: a test that admits unreadable copies admits fabrication, while a test that requires readable co
pies disqualifies the one party whose four-hundred-year record was genuine.
