\s35\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 Weinstein was summoned on the Friday, which was lawful now, and he came without being asked and stood while Mrs Kind read him pages five to eleven, and did not sit down at any point.
\par At the end he said, "He was correct in every particular."
\par "You lied to him," said Neville.
\par "On the first two occasions. Then he asked a third time, and nobody had asked me three times since Ravenna, and I told him the truth, and then I asked him not to write it down, and he refused, and he was right to refuse." Weinstein's hands were on the bac
k of the chair. "And I want to say the next thing to this whole room and I want it minuted before anybody is tempted to be sentimental about it. He died four months later and it had }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 
nothing to do with me}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
. He was ill. He had been ill for years, in a way his century treated as a defect of character. He had spent thirty years being told his life's work was a bookkeeping fiction by men with chairs. I will not have his death made into a consequence of a conve
rsation with me, because that would be a way of making it about me, and it was not about me, and I have watched the living do that to the dead for eleven thousand years and it is the second-worst thing they do."
\par Beatrix said, "What is the worst?"
\par "Filing it," said Halpert Weinstein.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi-14\li144\ri0\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin144\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
