\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang {\pntxta .}}{\*\pnseclvl4\pnlcltr\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang {\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl5\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang {\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl6\pnlcltr\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang {\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}
{\*\pnseclvl7\pnlcrm\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang {\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl8\pnlcltr\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang {\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl9\pnlcrm\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang {\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}\pard\plain \ltrpar
\s35\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 The physics of the ledger}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  took Ramanathan and Fainrose the weekend, and it produced the thing that changed the case.
\par "Soccermann's prediction is right and it was proved in nineteen sixty-one," said Ramanathan on Monday. "It's Landauer's principle, and we have used it twice already in this file without noticing that we were being handed something.
\par "A sorter \emdash  a demon, Maxwell's version, sitting at a shutter letting fast molecules one way and slow ones the other \emdash  does not get order for free. But the payment is not where anybody looked for eighty years. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 Measurement can in principle be free.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  The unavoidable cost is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 erasure}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid14645859 : clearing a bit of memory to make room for the next observation dissipates at least }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs38\f2\fs20\insrsid14645859 k_B T \\ln 2}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
. Bennett established that in nineteen eighty-two, and it has been measured directly \emdash 
 single-particle experiments have hit the Landauer bound, and other groups have run the demon in reverse and converted information into work at the predicted rate.
\par "So a demon with }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 infinite memory}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  is not impossible. It is simply not a perpetual engine. It runs, and it accumulates, and it never pays, and it }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 cannot}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  
pay, because the payment is forgetting and it has nothing to forget with. Its memory is the account. The second law is satisfied in the only way available: the entropy is not destroyed, it is stored in the one place nobody audits."
\par Fainrose said, "Eleven thousand years of it."
\par "Eleven thousand years of perfectly retained, unerasable discarded branches, and he can recite them, and he cannot stop reciting them when he is distressed, which a physicist in nineteen six recorded as evidence and everybody since has recorded as a manne
rism."
\par Neville said, "Is there any relief for him at all?"
\par "There is exactly one," said Ramanathan, "and it is worse than none. He could forget. And the moment he does, the stored entropy discharges into the world, all of it, at once, at whatever temperature he happens to be standing in." She looked up. "So the r
eason that creature has not permitted himself the smallest mercy in eleven thousand years is not discipline and it is not vanity. He is a full vessel standing in a room with people in it."
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi-14\li144\ri0\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin144\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
