\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 Chapter Twelve carries }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 statistical mechanics as Boltzmann built it}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 , the objections it survived, and the resolution of }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Maxwell's demon}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  through the thermodynamics of information.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Entropy as a count.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  Boltzmann's insight is that the thermodynamic entropy of a macrostate is a measure of how many microstates realise it:
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s41\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\tx916\tx1832\tx2748\tx3664\tx4580\tx5496\tx6412\tx7328\tx8244\tx9160\tx10076\tx10992\tx11908\tx12824\tx13740\tx14656\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 
\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs38\insrsid14645859 S = k_B \\ln W}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s35\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 where }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs38\f2\fs20\insrsid14645859 W}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
 is the number of microscopic configurations consistent with the macroscopic description. (The equation in this form, and the constant }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs38\f2\fs20\insrsid14645859 k_B}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
, are due to Planck; the tombstone in Vienna's Zentralfriedhof carries it, though Boltzmann never wrote it that way.) The consequence is that entropy is not a substance but a property of a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 
description}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 : it depends on the coarse-graining, on which distinctions the observer can actually make. This is the point the chapter's plot exploits, and it is also the resolution of the }{\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Gibbs paradox}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  \emdash  the entropy of mixing depends on whether the mixed species are distinguishable in principle.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Why the second law is statistical.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
 Given the count, the second law follows as overwhelming probability rather than necessity: high-entropy macrostates are realised by incomparably more microstates, with ratios of order }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs38\f2\fs20\insrsid14645859 10^
\{10^\{23\}\}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 , so a system wandering among accessible configurations will almost certainly be found in one of the numerous kind. Nothing prohibits the rare outcome.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 The two great objections, both correct.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  Boltzmann's 1872 }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 H-theorem}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  appeared to derive irreversibility from mechanics, and it relies on the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 Stosszahlansatz}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
, the assumption of uncorrelated molecular velocities before collision \emdash  a statistical input, not a mechanical one.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls19\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid5709733 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 
\ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Loschmidt (1876):}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  since the microscopic dynamics are time-reversal invariant, reversing all velocities produces an equally lawful evolution in which }{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs38\f2\fs20\insrsid14645859 H}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  increases. No purely mechanical derivation of the second law can therefore exist.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Zermelo (1896),}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  invoking Poincar\'e9 recurrence: a bounded, isolated system must return arbitrarily close to any prior state, so entropy cannot increase monotonically for ever.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s35\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
Boltzmann accepted both and reformulated accordingly: the law is probabilistic, entropy decreases are permitted but astronomically improbable at macroscopic scales, and low-entropy conditions require a separate account (Chapter Ten's Past Hypothesis).

\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 The vindication he did not live to see.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  Modern }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 fluctuation theorems}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  quantify exactly the improbability he was accused of hand-waving:
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls20\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid5709733 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 
\ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Evans\endash Searles (1993)}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  fluctuation theorem, giving the ratio of probabilities for entropy-producing and entropy-consuming trajectories.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Jarzynski equality (1997):}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs38\f2\fs20\insrsid14645859 \\langle e^\{-W/k_BT\}\\rangle = e^\{-\\Delta F/k_BT\}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
, valid for arbitrarily fast, far-from-equilibrium processes.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Crooks fluctuation theorem (1999)}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 , relating forward and reverse work distributions.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s35\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
These have been confirmed experimentally with optically trapped colloidal beads and with single-molecule RNA unfolding. Transient violations of the second law occur at small scales at precisely the predicted rates.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Maxwell's demon and where the account is paid.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
 Maxwell's 1867 sorting intelligence appears to produce order without work. Szilard's 1929 single-molecule engine sharpened it to a rate: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs38\f2\fs20\insrsid14645859 k_B T \\ln 2}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid14645859  of work extractable per bit of information about which side the molecule is on. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Landauer (1961)}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  located the compensating cost 
\emdash  not in measurement, but in }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 erasure}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 : resetting one bit of memory dissipates at least }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cs38\f2\fs20\insrsid14645859 k_B T \\ln 2}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 . }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Bennett (1982)}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
 completed the argument by showing measurement can in principle be performed reversibly, so the demon's books balance only when it clears its memory. The Landauer bound has since been measured directly in single-particle systems (B\'e9
rut et al., 2012), and the demon run in reverse to convert information into work at the predicted efficiency (Toyabe et al., 2010).
\par The chapter's use of this is exact: a demon with unbounded, never-erased memory violates nothing. It is not a perpetual-motion machine; it is a machine that never settles its account, storing the entropy it removes from the world as an unerasable internal
 record. Erasure would discharge that stored entropy as heat.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Certifying without reading.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  Van Casteel's proposal rests on the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Sagawa\endash 
Ueda generalised second law}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 , which extends thermodynamics to feedback control by an informed agent:
