 is the mutual information between the agent's record and the system. The extractable work is bounded by the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 correlation}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
, and mutual information is a relation between two physical systems, not a property of marks on a medium. Consequently a genuinely correlated archive contains extractable work proportional to its information content, while a fabricated one \emdash 
