\s35\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 The theorem}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  came after soup, and Drill did it standing, badly, and it was the most important twenty minutes in the chapter.
\par "There is a persistent story," he said, "that my rule was a philosophical preference which the Irishman's theorem later swept away. That is quite wrong and the record is available. What the Irishman's theorem killed was }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cs37\b\insrsid14645859 local hidden variables}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  \emdash 
 the idea that outcomes are fixed in advance by properties carried along, with no influence between wings. I never held that. The man who wrote the nineteen thirty-five paper }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 did}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 .
\par "And in nineteen sixty-seven two people proved the thing that is actually mine, and it has almost no public profile at all, and it should. They showed that you cannot assign definite, pre-existing values to all quantum observables at once, }{\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 even allowing any amount of nonlocality}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
, in any way that respects the algebraic relations between them. It is not a probabilistic result. It is not statistical. It requires no experiment involving distant wings and no assumption about locality whatever. It is a straightforward impossibility, a
nd what it establishes is that the value you get depends on }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 which other observables you chose to measure alongside it}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  \emdash 
 on the context, on the arrangement, on the bench.
\par "That is called contextuality. It is my rule with a proof attached. It has since been demonstrated in laboratories with photons and with ions and with single nuclear spins, and \emdash 
 this is the part I find funniest and I am too old to pretend otherwise \emdash  it turns out to be the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 resource}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
 that makes certain quantum computations faster than classical ones. My philosophical preference, which I was told for sixty years was Copenhagen mysticism, is currently being sold as a commodity."
\par Barbarian said, from the corner, "Then Weinstein's determinism is dead."
\par "No," said Drill, unhappily. "No, that is too fast and I will not have it. The theorem forbids }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 context-independent}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  
pre-existing values. It does not forbid determinism. There are fully deterministic accounts which survive it perfectly well by being explicitly contextual and explicitly nonlocal \emdash 
 your Duc's pilot wave from the first book is exactly such an account, and I have never had an argument against it beyond taste, and taste is not an argument, and I have said so in print twice.
\par "What the theorem forbids is the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 form of reasoning}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  
in your Chapter Three. It forbids saying: there was no waste on the vampire's bench, therefore the outcomes on the register's bench were fixed in advance. Because 'fixed in advance' is not a property a system carries about with it. It is a property of a s
ystem }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 together with an arrangement}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 , and you had two."
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi-14\li144\ri0\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin144\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
