{\*\pnseclvl7\pnlcrm\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang {\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl8\pnlcltr\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang {\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl9\pnlcrm\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang {\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}\pard\plain \ltrpar
\s35\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 The rescue}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  was Ramanathan's and it was expensive.
\par "If the objection is that we combined two benches," she said, "then the answer is not to argue. It is to }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 build one bench}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
. A single arrangement in which the branch-structure coupling and the outcome register are parts of the same characterised instrument, with a specified interaction, calibrated, repeatable, with the error budget written down."
\par "You cannot characterise him," said Miss Pike.
\par "I can characterise the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 coupling}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  
without understanding the mechanism. I do it with detectors I did not design every week of my life." Ramanathan looked at Weinstein, and then away, and then back, because she had decided something. "Mr Weinstein. To make Chapter Three admissible, you woul
d have to be incorporated. Formally. As departmental apparatus. Your feeding would be logged, gated, and referenced to the register, and every branch you consumed would be an entry in a calibration record, and you would be a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 schedule to the instrument list}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 ."
\par Weinstein said, "I have been many things."
\par "There is a consequence," said Beatrix, and she was already writing. "If he is departmental apparatus, then what he holds is departmental. And Chapter Twelve established what he holds." She stopped writing. "Neville. Eleven thousand years of unerasable st
ored entropy. Uncleared. Undischarged. On our instrument list."
\par Fainrose said, "The Crown inherits the ledger."
\par "The Crown inherits the ledger," said Beatrix, "and every discarded branch in it, and every question of whether it was needed, and the debt cannot be discharged because discharge means forgetting and forgetting means release into whatever room he is stand
ing in, and I would be advising the department to acquire, as a fixed asset, the largest single item of undisclosed liability in the history of the state."
\par There was quite a long silence.
\par Halpert Weinstein said, "May I say something in my own matter?"
\par "You may."
\par "Do it," he said. "Not because it is prudent. It is the least prudent thing anybody has proposed in two books and Ms Sloan is entirely right about the liability." He had his hands on the table. "Do it because for eleven thousand years I have been an instr
ument nobody characterised, and every wrong I have done has been possible because of that, and Mr Drill has just told this room that an uncharacterised instrument is not evidence but a lead. I should like to stop being a lead."
