\ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 The Fermi paper}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  
arrived from the Office of the President on the Thursday, and it was one page, and Neville read it out at the end of the day because he did not know what to do with it.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 
The Office observes that the Programme claims to have maintained subscription across the signatory volume for eleven thousand years, and that adequate subscription is said to be the precondition of records, of predictability, and of the emergence of compl
ex structure.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 The Office therefore invites the parties to explain why, in eleven thousand years, the Counsel has never once been contacted by a volume which maintained its own.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid14645859 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 
There are, on the parties' own figures, some hundreds of billions of stellar systems within the arm. The Office notes that the Programme's own maintenance rounds have never encountered evidence of an independent subscription authority, a competing registe
r, or a second Programme.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 The Office does not advance a conclusion. It merely observes that a service claiming to be indispensable has, in eleven thousand years, found no one else who thought so.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
\par Drill listened to it twice and then said, slowly, and revising as usual:
\par "That is \emdash  no. Let me say it the other way about. That is a good question badly asked, which is the most dangerous kind, and I am too old to be the person who answers it, but I will say one thing about its }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cs36\i\insrsid14645859 shape}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 .
\par "It asks why nobody has been found. Finding is a bench. Maintaining is a different bench. And I have spent thirty-six years being told by clients that because their instrument showed nothing, nothing was there, and I have made rather a good living out of 
the interval between those two statements." He got up, slowly, for his taxi. "Somebody in this department should ask what arrangement would be required to detect a volume that had maintained its own subscription, and whether it is compatible with the arra
ngement required to maintain yours. I suspect it is not. I have suspected it since nineteen seventy-one. I have no evidence and I would not dream of publishing."
\par Neville said, "Mr Drill \emdash  could I have that in writing?"
\par And Nelson Drill said, from the door, with what Neville was almost sure was satisfaction:
\par "You could not. I have never in my life said a sentence twice the same way and I have been assured by two governments that it makes me useless." He put his hat on. "Though I have noticed, Mr Wren, since you have a President who does his work with true sen
tences cut loose from the men who said them, that being impossible to quote is not the disadvantage everyone told me it was."
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi-14\li144\ri0\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin144\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
