\s35\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 Neville wrote, that night:
\par Drill: the finding may be right and the route is not permitted.\line An error can be found. An invalid route cannot.
\par Then:
\par 1935: I could have predicted either, and I disturbed nothing, therefore both were there.\line The ambiguity is in 'disturbing'. Nothing is jogged. But the choice fixes what kind of claim is available.\line 
Two mutually exclusive arrangements are not two accounts of one situation.\line The phenomenon is the system AND the instrument. You may not carve off the instrument and call the rest a property.
\par Then, underlined:
\par We disposed of a cousin of his rule and came home thinking we had disposed of his.\line 1967: no context-independent pre-existing values, even allowing unlimited nonlocality. No locality assumption. Not statistical.\line 
Contextuality. His preference with a proof attached. Now sold as a computing resource.\line It does not kill determinism. Pilot wave survives. It kills our ROUTE.
\par Then:
\par Restated his way, Chapter Three gets worse, not weaker:\line there is no fact about which options a state 'has' apart from the arrangement that defines them.\line THE REGISTER WAS THE ARRANGEMENT.\line We did not fail to notice her doors had closed.\line 
We were the apparatus that determined what counted as a door,\line and while ours was the only bench in the room the question had no answer.
\par Beatrix will advise the nine of that on Friday. She did not hesitate for one second.
\par Then:
\par Rescue: build one bench. Characterise the instrument.\line Incorporate him. Log the feeding. Reference it to the register.\line Consequence: the Crown inherits the ledger. Undischargeable. Largest undisclosed liability in the history of the state.\line 
He said do it anyway. 'I should like to stop being a lead.'
\par Then, the Fermi paper:
\par 'A service claiming to be indispensable has, in eleven thousand years, found no one else who thought so.'\line Drill: finding is a bench, maintaining is a different bench.\line Ask whether the arrangement needed to DETECT a self-maintained volume\line 
is compatible with the arrangement needed to maintain ours.\line He suspects not. Since 1971. No evidence. Would not dream of publishing.
\par And last:
\par He cannot say a sentence the same way twice.\line Two governments told him it made him useless.\line It is the only defence against our President that anybody has found.
\par 68 days.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s2\ql \fi-14\li144\ri0\sb160\sa80\sl259\slmult1\keep\keepn\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin0\lin144\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31503\afs32\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs32\cf19\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\loch\af31502\hich\af31502\dbch\af31501\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31503 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 \hich\af31502\dbch\af31501\loch\f31502 Physics
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s35\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 Chapter Thirteen carries }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Bohr's reply to EPR}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 , 
}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 complementarity}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  as a claim about experimental arrangements, and the theorem that eventually vindicated it: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Kochen\endash Specker contextuality}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 .
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 The EPR argument.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  
Einstein, Podolsky and Rosen (1935) proposed a criterion of reality: "If, without in any way disturbing a system, we can predict with certainty the value of a physical quantity, then there exists an element of physical reality corresponding to that quanti
ty." Applied to an entangled pair, a position measurement on one wing permits certain prediction of the distant particle's position; a momentum measurement permits certain prediction of its momentum. Since either could have been chosen and neither disturb
s the far particle, EPR concluded that both quantities are real, and that quantum mechanics \emdash  which cannot assign both \emdash  is incomplete.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Bohr's reply.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
 Bohr answered in Physical Review the same year, under the same title, and located the flaw in the phrase "without in any way disturbing." He conceded there is no mechanical disturbance of the distant system. His claim is that the choice of measurement on
 the near wing determines "the very conditions which define the possible types of predictions regarding the future behaviour of the system." The two experimental arrangements \emdash  one suited to position, one to momentum \emdash  are }{\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 mutually exclusive as hardware}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
, and results obtained under one may not be combined with results obtainable only under the other as if both described a single state of affairs. This is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 complementarity}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 : certain pairs of properties, position and momentum, or interference and which-path information, require arrangements that cannot be realised together, and the object of description is the whole }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 phenomenon}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  \emdash  system plus apparatus \emdash 
 rather than a property of the system alone. Bohr's presentation is notoriously difficult, and the obscurity of his prose has generated a century of dispute about exactly what he meant; the chapter's characterisation of it as a ru
le about benches is a defensible reading and is the reading with the clearest physical content.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 The scorecard, which is frequently misreported.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  Bell's theorem refuted }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 
local hidden variables}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  \emdash 
 the assumption that outcomes are determined by properties carried along, without influence between wings. EPR assumed exactly that; Bohr did not. So Bell's result told against Einstein's position, not Bohr's. What vindicated Bohr's own claim came in 196
7.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Kochen\endash Specker.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  
Kochen and Specker (building on Gleason and on an argument of Bell's from 1966) proved that it is impossible to assign definite, pre-existing values to all quantum observables simultaneously in a way that respects their algebraic relations \emdash 
 specifically, that preserves functional relationships among commuting observables. The result is:
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls22\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid5709733 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 
\ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 not statistical}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  \emdash  it is a straightforward impossibility, not an inequality;
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 independent of locality}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  \emdash  it requires no separated wings and permits arbitrary nonlocality;
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 finite}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid14645859  \emdash  the original proof used 117 vectors in three dimensions; smaller sets are now known.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s35\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 Its content is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 contextuality}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
: the value obtained for an observable cannot be independent of which other compatible observables are measured alongside it. That is complementarity with a proof attached. Contextuality has been demonstrated experimentally with photons, trapped ions, neu
trons and single nuclear spins, and \emdash  as the chapter notes with some relish \emdash  it is now understood as a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 resource}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  
for quantum computational advantage, notably in magic-state distillation schemes.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 What contextuality does and does not forbid.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  It rules out context-independent value assignments. It does not rule out determinism. }{\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 De Broglie\endash Bohm pilot-wave theory}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  
(Book One, Chapter Twelve) is fully deterministic and survives, precisely because it is explicitly contextual and explicitly nonlocal: measured outcomes depend on the whole experimental configuration, not on a pre-existing value carried by the particle al
one. What contextuality forbids is the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 inferential move}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  \emdash 
 reasoning from a result obtained under one arrangement to a conclusion about what was fixed in advance under another.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Two distinct complementarities.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  
The chapter is careful about a real conflation. Bohr's complementarity concerns mutually exclusive measurement arrangements and is a claim about how quantum phenomena must be described. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 
Black hole complementarity}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  
(Susskind, Thorlacius and Uglum, 1993; Chapter Five) is a much stronger and more speculative conjecture: that the exterior and interior accounts of a horizon are each complete and may never be compared. The AMPS firewall argument, resting on monogamy of e
ntanglement, tells against the latter. It leaves Bohr's rule entirely untouched.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 Why the plot consequence follows.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  
If a system's properties are defined only relative to an arrangement, then the register that specified two permitted options was not a passive record of doors that existed; it was the apparatus that determined what counted as a door. That is a strictly st
ronger indictment than negligent monitoring, and it is the correct reading of contextuality applied to the book's fiction. The remedy \emdash  characterising the uncharacterised instrument, so that both observations belong to one specified arrangement 
\emdash  is also the right methodological instinct, and its cost in the story is the point: an instrument that has never been calibrated is not evidence, and making it evidence means taking responsibility for everything it holds.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s3\ql \fi-14\li144\ri0\sb160\sa80\sl259\slmult1\keep\keepn\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin0\lin144\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31503\afs28\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs28\cf19\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\loch\af31506\hich\af31506\dbch\af31501\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31503 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31501\loch\f31506 What the reader learns
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls23\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid5709733 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 EPR's criterion of reality, and its inference that both position and momentum must pre-exist because either could be predicted with certainty.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
Bohr's reply locates the ambiguity in "without in any way disturbing": the choice of arrangement fixes what kinds of claims are meaningful, without mechanical disturbance.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
Complementarity concerns mutually exclusive experimental arrangements; the phenomenon includes the apparatus and cannot be split into system-property plus instrument.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}Bell refuted local hidden variables, which was EPR's assumption rather than Bohr's.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}Kochen\endash Specker (1967) proves no context-independent value assignment exists \emdash 
 non-statistical, locality-free, and finite.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}Contextuality is experimentally confirmed and is now treated as a computational resource.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}Contextuality does not exclude determinism; pilot-wave theory survives by being contextual and nonlocal.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
Bohr's complementarity and black hole complementarity are different claims; refuting the second leaves the first standing.
