\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 Fainrose, who had read the file overnight, said carefully, "Dr Esaki. Might I ask what you did, before we ask you why you're here?"
\par "I grew crystals," said Esaki. "Very heavily doped. Degenerate semiconductor on both sides of a junction, so heavily doped that the depletion region \emdash  the barrier, if you like your word \emdash 
 was thin. A few nanometres. Thinner than any barrier has any business being if you expect a particle to go over it in the ordinary way, by having enough energy to climb.
\par "And I applied a small voltage, in the reverse direction from what any sensible engineer expected current to flow, and current flowed. Backwards. Before the voltage was large enough to explain it by any classical route. I did not have a name for it at fir
st. Later we called it tunnelling, because the particle did not climb the barrier. It appeared on the other side without having been anywhere in between that would show a trace of having climbed."
\par Mrs Kind said, "That is the word this department has been arguing about since March."
\par "I know," said Esaki. "It is why I am here. The nine did not send me to review your Chapter One. Your Chapter One is correct. They sent me because your Chapter One is correct and everybody in this building has spent thirteen chapters being astonished by i
t, and I am ninety-one years old and I have run out of patience with astonishment."
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi-14\li144\ri0\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin144\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
