\s35\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 Mrs Kind, who had been quiet, said: "Dr Esaki. May I ask a travel agent's question."
\par "You built a business on holidays," said Esaki, without looking up. "Mr Drill told me. Ask."
\par "When somebody books a package to a country they can't legally enter \emdash  visa refused, papers wrong, the whole booking is a fiction on both ends \emdash 
 I don't say they travelled there illegally. I say the booking never described a real trip. It described two un
connected facts wearing a single itinerary." She leaned forward. "Is that what you mean? That most of what people call tunnelling isn't a mysterious crossing at all \emdash 
 it's proof that the 'barrier' the paperwork describes was never a real barrier to begin with?"
\par "That," said Esaki, and for the first time all day something happened to his face that might have been pleasure, "is a better statement of it than I gave the Swedish committee. Yes. A tunnelling event is not evidence that something impossible happened. It
 is evidence that your classical description of what was possible was wrong, and the wave was, all along, more honest about the geography than your barrier was."
\par Fainrose said, slowly, "Then the fourteen weren't proof that the register's barrier failed. They're proof the register's barrier was never\emdash "
\par "I have not read your register," said Esaki
, "and at ninety-one I do not intend to start. I have told you what a barrier is. What you do with fourteen files that crossed one is your department's business, not a semiconductor's." He stood, declining help. "Though I will say, since your Mr Drill is 
a man I respect and he is not here to stop me \emdash  if your instrument was never characterised, you do not yet know whether you are describing a barrier at all. You may simply be describing a place where you stopped looking."
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi-14\li144\ri0\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin144\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
