\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 He left before tea could be offered a second time, refusing again, and the driver \emdash  a different one \emdash 
 was already at the kerb, and Neville watched from the window as Esaki got in without assistance and the car pulled away toward whatever remained of his Monday.
\par Ramanathan said, into the quiet, "He just did to Chapter One what Drill did to Chapter Three."
\par "No," said Fainrose. "Drill told us our route was invalid. Esaki told us we might not have a barrier at all, and that if we do, crossing it was never the anomaly \emdash 
 the register's confidence that it couldn't be crossed was the anomaly, and it was ours."
\par Beatrix had already opened a new folder. "Then I need to know, before Friday, whether the 'permitted options' in that register describe a real forbidden amplitude, or whether we built a diode and called the thing on the far side a crime."
