\s35\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 Neville wrote, that night:
\par Esaki: a barrier is not a wall.\line A barrier is a region where the classical description says the amplitude should be zero, and it is not.\line It does not care what it is made of. Nanometres of crystal, a mountain in a nucleus, a line in a register.

\par The particle is not a traveller who cheated a toll.\line There is no loan. No ledger entry. No lender.\line Strike 'borrowed energy' from every report. I have read it in three.
\par Then, underlined:
\par Not crossed by having enough.\line Crossed by never entirely being on one side to begin with.
\par Then, Mrs Kind's version, which he liked better and said so in the margin:
\par A booking to a country you cannot enter is not an illegal trip.\line It is proof the itinerary never described a real journey.\line Ask whether our register describes a real barrier\line or a place where we stopped looking and called it a wall.
\par Then:
\par If your instrument was never characterised, you do not know whether you are describing a barrier at all.\line Drill said the same thing about Weinstein in different words and neither of them knows the other said it.
\par Then:
\par Esaki refused tea twice. Refused help into the car twice.\line Ninety-one, and the only thing he came here to correct was our astonishment.
\par And last:
\par Beatrix wants to know by Friday whether the register describes an amplitude or a wall we stopped looking past.
\par 68 days. No \emdash  Ramanathan says thirty-one cores are still advancing. I should ask her what that means for the count.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s2\ql \fi-14\li144\ri0\sb160\sa80\sl259\slmult1\keep\keepn\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin0\lin144\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31503\afs32\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
