\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls25\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid5709733 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 Esaki's 1957 tunnel diode: reverse-bias current in a heavily doped p-n junction, explained by quantum tunnelling, shared the 1973 Nobel Prize.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
Tunnelling is not energy "borrowed" and "paid back"; the wavefunction has genuine non-zero amplitude on both sides of a finite barrier as one continuous solution.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
A classically forbidden region is one where the potential exceeds total energy; the wavefunction decays there but need not vanish, and resumes oscillating past a finite barrier.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}The same mechanism explains alpha decay, scanning tunnelling microscopy, and stellar fusion \emdash 
 one equation, arbitrarily many "barriers."
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
A barrier is properly defined as a region where a classical description predicts zero amplitude and the true amplitude is not zero \emdash  a claim about amplitude, not geography.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid14645859 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
Whether a given register or boundary is a genuine amplitude-barrier or merely the limit of an uncharacterised instrument's detection is an empirical question, not a metaphysical one.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s3\ql \fi-14\li144\ri0\sb160\sa80\sl259\slmult1\keep\keepn\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin0\lin144\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31503\afs28\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
