\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 The letter did not come from the nine, or from the Office, or from any living correspondent, and that was the first thing wrong with it.
\par It came from the registry's oldest holding, an envelope catalogued in 1917 and never opened because the docket said }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 hold pending confirmation of addressee's survival}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid14645859 , and nobody, in over a century, had thought to check whether the confirmation had ever arrived. Mrs Kind found it while looking for something else entirely, read the covering slip, and brought it to Fainrose without a word.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 From: Lt. K. Schwarzschild, Russian Front.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 \line }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 
To: whichever office of His Majesty's Government concerns itself with the shape of things.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 \line }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 
Enclosed: a solution, obtained between duties, to Herr Einstein's field equations, for the case of a single point mass. I do not expect to require it returned.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
\par He was right. He did not require it returned. He died of a rare autoimmune disease contracted at the front a few months after posting it, having spent his final active weeks doing exact general relativity by lamplight between artillery calculations, and t
he solution reached Einstein, who was startled that anyone had found an exact answer to his own approximate one so quickly, and who read it to the Prussian Academy on the dead man's behalf.
\par What had never reached anyone, until Mrs Kind opened it, was the second half of the letter, which Karl Schwarzschild had apparently thought too speculative to send to Einstein and had sent instead, for reasons the file did not explain, to "whichever offic
e concerns itself with the shape of things" \emdash  an office that, in 1917, was the direct institutional ancestor of the Ministry.
