\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 Ramanathan had gone very still. "That is not merely tunnelling," she said. "That is the other thing. That is the thing Weinstein's horizon has been doing to my instruments for six months and I called it noise."
\par "Say it properly," said Fainrose.
\par "His solution \emdash  the real Schwarzschild solution, maximally extended, which nobody worked out fully until nineteen sixty \emdash  does not describe one hole. Extended honestly, the maths gives you }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cs37\b\insrsid14645859 two}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  
asymptotically flat regions, joined at a throat, at a single instant, with the throat pinching shut faster than anything could cross it. A bridge between two elsewheres that exists for less time than it would take to use.
\par "And your fourteen went missing on the fourteenth of March. Not destroyed \emdash 
 Chapter One was careful about that, and Chapter Twelve gave us a place for what's consumed and what's stored. But there was a residue nobody could source, in Ramanathan's words from March, that behaved like it belonged to two files at once."
\par Miss Pike said, slowly, "Are you saying the fourteen went through a wormhole?"
\par "I am saying," said Ramanathan, "that a lieutenant of artillery worked out, in a trench, in 1916, using nothing but Einstein's equations and appalling personal circumstances, that any object heavy enough to have a horizon at all }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 necessarily}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
 comes with a second region attached to it in the mathematics, whether or not anyone can reach it, and Halpert Weinstein has had a horizon for eleven thousand years."
\par Weinstein, summoned again, arrived within the hour, and for once did not sit.
\par "I have never used it," he said. "I want that said before anyone asks the question shaped like an accusation. I did not know it was there in the sense your lieutenant means. I knew there was a place behind me I do not go, and I assumed, as anyone assumes 
of the inside of their own throat, that it was simply }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 more of me}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  \emdash 
 darkness, mine, private, unremarkable. Nobody had told me it was, structurally, a second building."
