\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
Fainrose had the Cumbrian records out within the hour, and it was van Casteel who put the shape of it together, because he was the one who had spent nineteen years thinking about what could be measured across a gap nothing should cross.
\par "A throat that pinches shut before anything can cross it is not useful to anyone," he said. "That is the classical Schwarzschild wormhole and it has always been a curiosity rather than a route \emdash 
 not traversable, not even in principle, because the geometry
 collapses the passage faster than light could carry a signal through it. Every physicist since nineteen sixty has said the same thing: lovely mathematics, no application, don't build anything on it.
\par "But there is a way to hold a throat open. You need something threading it with negative energy density \emdash 
 a substance that violates the ordinary energy conditions, that gravitates the wrong way, propping the corridor rather than letting it collapse.
\par "And Chapter Two of this department's own casework identified precisely such a substance, and none of you noticed, because you filed it under vacuum energy and moved on." He looked at Fainrose. "Casimir energy is negative. I have measured it directly with
 plates a fraction of a millimetre apart for nineteen years. It is small. It is laughably small, by the standard of what you would need to prop open a throat between galaxies. But it is not zero, and it is not hypothetical, and it is the one substance in 
this department's files that has the correct sign."
\par The room was very quiet.
\par "You are not proposing we built one," said Beatrix carefully.
\par "I am proposing," said van Casteel, "that something has been holding a throat open behind Mr Weinstein for eleven thousand years using exactly the resource this department has spent two chapters measuring in a Cumbrian mineshaft, and that nobody thought t
o ask what a horizon eleven millennia old, fed continuously, and never once permitted to evaporate, might have had time to become on the inside."
