\ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 What it meant for the case}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 , Beatrix laid out on the Wednesday, grim about it.
\par "If van Casteel is right that something has propped Weinstein's throat open for eleven millennia using a Casimir-sign resource, then the second asymptotic region behind him is not a mathematical curiosity. It is a place. It has been a place for eleven tho
usand years, unaudited, unvisited, and \emdash  if the fourteen went somewhere on the fourteenth of March that this department could not source \emdash  possibly not empty."
\par "You think the fourteen are through it," said Miss Pike.
\par "I think," said Beatrly, "that we have spent fifteen chapters asking whether fourteen files were destroyed, stored, or forgiven, and Lieutenant Schwarzschild has just handed us a fourth category from a trench in 1916, which is that they were }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 posted}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 , and the address on the other end has never once been checked, because until this morning nobody in this building knew there was another end."

\par Ramanathan was already reaching for the Cumbrian instruments. "Then I need to know if a throat held open by a Casimir-sign source is traversable enough for a resolved amplitude to pass through it, or only large enough for the mathematics to be technically
 true and practically useless."
\par "That," said van Casteel, standing, "is a bench I can build."
