\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
The bench van Casteel had promised took eleven days to build and forty minutes to use, and the forty minutes settled more of the book's business than the eleven days had led anyone to expect.
\par He did it in Cumbria, in the mineshaft, with two plates, a torsion balance recalibrated to Ramanathan's specification, and a length of superconducting cable run down from the surface for no reason he ever fully explained except that he said a man is entit
led to one extravagance per experiment and this was his.
\par "The measurement is simple to state and was hateful to build," he said, over the telephone, at half past six in the morning, to a room that had come in specially. "I am not measuring Mr Weinstein. I could not get near enough to matter, and would not wish 
to. I am measuring the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 plates}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 , and inferring the rest, which is the only kind of measurement I have ever trusted.
\par "If there is a throat behind that horizon, propped by a negative energy density, then the vacuum in its vicinity is not the ordinary vacuum. It has a sign correction. And a sign correction, however small, changes the force between two plates held near eno
ugh to it by a calculable amount, and I have spent eleven days building an instrument sensitive to a correction of the size I expect and not one order of magnitude more, because more than that and I would be hallucinating a wormhole to make the numbers wo
rk, and I am too old for that particular vanity."
\par The plates moved by four hundred and eleven attometres. Van Casteel read the figure out twice, apologised for his voice doing something unprofessional on the second reading, and then said the sentence that ended the argument:
\par "It is there. It is real. And it is holding open a corridor perhaps the width of an atomic nucleus, for a duration I cannot yet bound, and I want everybody in that room to understand what that means before anyone gets excited. A throat that wide is not a 
door. It is not a route. Fourteen resolved amplitudes did not walk through an opening the width of a nucleus any more than the tide walks through a keyhole. If they went anywhere, they did not go as travellers. They went as }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \cs37\b\insrsid14645859 information}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  \emdash 
 correlations, threaded through, at a rate so far below anything a person or a signal could use that Lieutenant Schwarzschild's own caution turns out to be exactly right twice over. There is a bridge. It has always been a bridge. It has never for one ins
tant been a road."
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi-14\li144\ri0\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin144\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
