\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 
Ramanathan took the four hundred and eleven attometres and the mutual-information bound from Chapter Twelve and put them together on the whiteboard, and it was the last physics of the book, and she did it slowly because she wanted everyone to see the arit
hmetic rather than take it from her.
\par "A throat this narrow, held open this long, can carry information at a rate bounded by its own tiny cross-section \emdash 
 and van Casteel's negative energy density gives me that cross-section to nine figures. I have run it against the fourteen's missing residue
 from March." She wrote the number and underlined it once. "It matches. Not approximately. To within instrument error.
\par "The fourteen were not destroyed. They were not, in Beatrix's earlier phrase, }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs36\i\insrsid14645859 drained}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859  
in the sense of lost to nothing. Every discarded branch, every correlation Weinstein did not keep for himself and did not deposit in the Cumbrian store, went down a throat the width of a nucleus, at a rate slower than this department's slowest form, into 
whatever is on the other side of a horizon eleven thousand years old.
\par "I cannot tell you what is there. Nobody can, not from this end, and the whole point of the last fifteen chapters is that I am no longer willing to guess. But I can tell you it is not nothing, because a throat with a genuine negative-energy prop is not a 
mathematical curiosity \emdash  van Casteel measured a force, not a possibility \emdash 
 and I can tell you it has been receiving a slow, narrow, faithful trickle of everything this Ministry ever failed to keep, for eleven thousand years, and calling it a filing error undersells it considerably."
\par Miss Pike said, quietly, "Then where did they go?"
\par "Somewhere," said Ramanathan, "that has been receiving this department's discards since before this department existed, and has never once written back, and I would very much like this book to end with somebody asking why not, rather than pretending we ha
ve answered it."
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi-14\li144\ri0\sl259\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin144\itap0\pararsid14645859 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
