\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid14645859 He wrote, at his desk, on the ninth of February, with the whole department very quiet around him and Weinstein \emdash  who had asked to be present, and been permitted, on Article Two's new terms \emdash 
 standing by the window with his hands behind his back and no reflection in the glass he was looking through:
\par We opened a letter that had waited a hundred and nine years for someone to check a box.\line We built an instrument to measure a man nobody had characterised in eleven thousand years.\line 
We found nine files that were never lost, only currently between two places at once,\line and decided, for once, not to force an answer the paperwork had no box for.
\par Then:
\par Van Casteel's plates moved four hundred and eleven attometres and he apologised for his voice.\line Fainrose: not lost, not drained. A very slow drain, into a very old pipe, that the Crown can finally insure.\line 
Ramanathan's number has not moved in six weeks. For a countdown, that is a celebration.
\par Then, underlined:
\par Weinstein asked to be held to something before anyone required it of him.\line It is the only sentence in either book where he went first.
\par Then:
\par Mrs Kell: a person who proposes the sensible answer should not also get to vote for it.\line I am going to try to remember that longer than I remember most things this department has taught me.
\par And last, because it was the only entry that mattered on this particular day:
\par Nothing detonated.\line Nobody was uninvited.\line The register closed clean, at 411 P-9, with an appendix nobody was ashamed to sign.
\par There is no countdown tomorrow. I find I do not know what to do with a morning that doesn't have one.
